// "Raises the reanimated husk as an obedient thrall, mindlessly carrying out
// the commands of the one who roused it" -- a genuine fighting/following
// minion, not a decorative phantasm. Every already-shipped player-spell
// `BasicSummon` (illusion/{minor_illusion_image,silent_image,major_image,
// project_image}.ron, transmutation/floating_disk.ron) is a
// `with_agent: false`, `incorporeal: true`, `phantom_illusion: true`,
// `has_health: false` decoy -- none is an actual owned, hittable, acting
// creature. This spell instead uses the OTHER already-real `SummonInfo::Npc`
// recipe, the one NPC-cast summon abilities already use for genuine owned
// companions (assets/common/abilities/custom/dwarves/forgemaster/
// summon_iron_dwarf.ron, assets/common/abilities/vampire/bloodmoon_heiress/
// summon.ron): `alignment`/`with_agent`/`incorporeal`/`phantom_illusion`/
// `delete_after_expiry` left at their `#[serde(default)]` values --
// `alignment: None` resolves to `Alignment::Owned(caster)`, `with_agent`
// defaults to true (real AI, matching "carrying out the commands"),
// `incorporeal`/`phantom_illusion` default to false (a real, hittable
// creature), `duration: None` means no expiry timer (a raised thrall stays
// until dismissed/killed, matching the sheet's classification as a
// persistent summon mechanic rather than a timed one). `loadout_config:
// None` -- `basic_summon.rs`'s own `with_default_maintool(body)` still gives
// the reanimated body its species-default weapon; no `Preset::*Summon`
// variant exists for an undead body and adding one is Rust (Lane B), out of
// scope for this content-only pass.
//
// `body`: `BipedSmall(Husk)` -- Necromancy's own already-shipped dungeon
// undead (assets/common/entity/dungeon/cultist/husk.ron), a real
// `CreatureKind::Undead` species (common/src/comp/body/mod.rs), and the
// literal "shambling husk" the sheet's own description names.
//
// KNOWN GAP, same one the Conjuration Wave-1 pilot (find_familiar.ron)
// documents and deliberately leaves open in this content-only pass:
// `Alignment::Owned` alone does not grant cross-session persistence (the
// real `comp::Pet`/DB-save/chunk-anchor path is untouched by `BasicSummon`),
// and nothing here caps or replaces a prior summon on recast -- repeated
// casts stack multiple thralls. A Lane B follow-up wiring `BasicSummon`
// through the real pet system would close this for every spell using this
// recipe, not just this one.
//
// `loadout_config`/`skillset_config`: `Preset::HuskSummon` already exists
// for this exact body (loadout_builder.rs) and is already used by the
// mechanically-identical conjuration/summon_shadowspawn.ron -- reused here
// instead of leaving the thrall unarmed.
BasicSummon(
    buildup_duration: 1.0,
    cast_duration: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    summon_info: Npc(
        summoned_amount: 1,
        summon_distance: (1.0, 2.0),
        body: BipedSmall((species: Husk, body_type: Male)),
        scale: None,
        has_health: true,
        use_npc_name: true,
        loadout_config: Some(HuskSummon),
        skillset_config: Some(Rank5),
        duration: None,
    ),
    meta: (school: Some(Necromancy), source: Some(Arcane), cooldown: Some(30.0)),
)
